'''BdSC Corporació''' ({{lang|ca|Corporació de la Borsa de Sant Cristòfor}}) is a [[Balboa|Balboan]] financial markets infrastructure company. It is the parent company of the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]], the [[Balboa Comerciants Exchange]], and [[ECD (Corporació de canvi de moneda de Balboa)|ECD]], and operates the country's principal equities, derivatives, and foreign-exchange markets from its headquarters in [[El Centre (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|El Centre]], [[Original]].

The company was founded on 5 March 1952 by [[Jonas Martin]], a [[Volisania|Volisanian]] investment banker who purchased the rights to the Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor from the [[Adonian Community]] receivership for $1,000,000 (International dollars). The Bolsa had been in AC receivership since the end of the [[Great Adonian War]], and Martin's acquisition gave him control of what was then a dormant exchange. Under his leadership, the Bolsa was reopened and modernised, and the group subsequently expanded into derivatives and foreign exchange.

The company is dual-listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and the [[Ampuria Stock Exchange]] in [[Volisania]]. The [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]], the Balboan sovereign direct investment fund, holds an 18 per cent stake in the company.

== Subsidiaries ==

=== Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor ===

{{main|Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor}}

The Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor is the principal securities market of [[Balboa]], handling listed equities and corporate bonds. Founded in 1903, it is the country's main venue for capital formation and the home of the [[SCX 30]] benchmark index.

=== Balboa Comerciants Exchange ===

The '''Balboa Comerciants Exchange''' is the group's derivatives and securities marketplace, handling futures, options, and other derivative instruments tied to Balboan equities, commodities, and interest rates.

=== ECD (Corporació de canvi de moneda de Balboa) ===

'''ECD''' ({{lang|ca|Corporació de canvi de moneda de Balboa}}) is the group's foreign-exchange operation, providing currency exchange and FX trading services for the Balboan market.

== Dual listing ==

BdSC Corporació is dual-listed on the Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor and the [[Ampuria Stock Exchange]] in [[Ampuria]], [[Volisania]]. The Volisania listing reflects the historical links between Balboa's financial system and the Illypnian capital markets, and provides the company with access to a deeper pool of international investors.

